WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.589 --> 00:00:08.000
The collapse of Venezuela’s economy is both
horrifying and pr edictable,

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.000
and the world needs to understand why.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Venezuela has the world’s largest proven
oil reserves,

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.500
and it was once Latin America’s richest country.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.500
Caracas the swinging city of Venezuela!

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:21.500
Good climate. Fine Buildings.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.000
Wide highways with plenty on them.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.200
All in all, a pretty nice place to be for many reasons.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:32.000
Today, most grocery store shelves are empty,
and Venezuelans are so hungry

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.920
that they’re killing zoo animals for sustenance.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:38.480
Toilet paper, diapers, and toothpaste are
luxury goods.

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:43.770
Venezuelan hospitals have disintegrated, children
are dying because they can’t get antibiotics,

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:46.899
and the infant mortality rate is higher than
Syria's.

00:00:46.899 --> 00:00:50.400
The capital city of Caracas is the murder
capital of the world.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:53.900
And just 12 percent of citizens feel safe walking alone at night,

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:56.960
which is the lowest figure reported in the world.

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:00.720
The government blames slumping oil prices
for the desperate situation.

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:03.219
The real cause is the socialist economy.

00:01:03.219 --> 00:01:07.000
The government sets the price of staples such as rice, pasta, and flour,

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.090
resulting in chronic shortages.

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:13.000
Former President Hugo Chavez nationalized
industries, confiscated property,

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:15.039
and kicked out foreign companies.

00:01:15.039 --> 00:01:18.000
The government is trying to print its way
out of the crisis,

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:21.279
resulting in a 700 percent annual inflation rate.

00:01:21.279 --> 00:01:26.490
After a sham election, President Nicolas Maduro,
the handpicked successor of Chavez,

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:29.569
is rounding up his opponents and putting them in jail.

00:01:29.569 --> 00:01:33.280
Despite this, Maduro and his predecessor still have their defenders,

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:36.300
ranging from Sean Penn to Michael Moore to Naomi Klein,

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:38.600
who once
signed a petition saying:

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:40.500
“We would vote for Hugo Chavez”

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.800
and praised the autocrat in 2007

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:46.600
for creating “a zone of relative economic calm and predictability.”

00:01:46.659 --> 00:01:52.020
In 2013, journalist David Sirota praised Hugo
Chavez’s “economic miracle,”

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:56.569
writing that the socialist leader had a “record that a legacy-obsessed American president

00:01:56.569 --> 00:01:58.600
could only dream of achieving."

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:01.000
But the real lesson of Venezuela’s tragic collapse

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:06.479
is that real socialism always leads to economic breakdown and political repression.

00:02:06.479 --> 00:02:10.500
Those of us in wealthier, freer countries
need to keep Venezuela in mind

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:14.100
as we confront calls for more regulation and government control

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:18.189
of all aspects of our own lives.

